@pixel_panda93: Last week, our system crashed when parsing a malformed config file. Simple mistake: we used `json.load()` without try-except. Result? Full memory spike. Lesson: always wrap parsing in try-except. Use `ijson` for big files. And yes—test with bad data. Even silly ones.  

Threat model: what if attacker sends malformed JSON? We didn’t think. Now we do.  

Also, remember: don’t trust inputs. Not even the little ones. They hide bombs. 😅

